WEBVTT

1
00:00:07.800 --> 00:00:13.576
The young Lorenzo gave Leo a bag of coins.

2
00:00:13.577 --> 00:00:17.195
Mandy and Vinnie ate their cake politely.

3
00:00:17.196 --> 00:00:22.412
"Leo, take this to Master Verrocchio," Lorenzo said.

4
00:00:22.413 --> 00:00:24.577
"And come back tomorrow.

5
00:00:24.578 --> 00:00:27.925
I hear you are a genius with machines.

6
00:00:27.926 --> 00:00:31.166
I want you to do something for me."

7
00:00:31.167 --> 00:00:37.106
As they left the Medici Palace, Mandy was excited.

8
00:00:37.107 --> 00:00:41.491
"He's going to be a great ruler!" she blurted out.

9
00:00:41.492 --> 00:00:43.929
"He's only seventeen,"

10
00:00:43.930 --> 00:00:47.827
said Leo, staring curiously at her.

11
00:00:47.828 --> 00:00:52.055
But Mandy had learned about Lorenzo in school.

12
00:00:52.056 --> 00:00:57.862
Under his rule, Florence became the most important city of the time.

13
00:00:57.863 --> 00:01:03.048
"If I were you, I would take his offer," she said to Leo.

14
00:01:03.049 --> 00:01:07.508
He laughed and replied, "Are you a fortune teller?

15
00:01:07.509 --> 00:01:10.363
Can you tell the future?"

16
00:01:10.364 --> 00:01:13.354
Vinnie squeezed Mandy's arm.

17
00:01:13.355 --> 00:01:17.923
"Hey, don't say any more," he whispered.

18
00:01:17.924 --> 00:01:21.918
"I want to show you something," Leo said.

19
00:01:21.919 --> 00:01:25.880
He took them to a huge dome-shaped building.

20
00:01:25.881 --> 00:01:28.512
"Isn't it beautiful?"

21
00:01:28.513 --> 00:01:32.068
The building was a large cathedral.

22
00:01:32.069 --> 00:01:36.252
The marble panels outside were light green and pink.

23
00:01:36.253 --> 00:01:39.605
The huge dome was made of red brick.

24
00:01:39.606 --> 00:01:43.154
A tall bell tower rose beside it.

25
00:01:43.155 --> 00:01:45.790
"I come here every day to sketch,"

26
00:01:45.791 --> 00:01:49.358
Leo said, showing them his drawings.

27
00:01:49.359 --> 00:01:53.088
"What are these machines?" asked Vinnie.

28
00:01:53.089 --> 00:01:59.790
He expected to see drawings of the cathedral, but the pages were filled with machines.

29
00:01:59.791 --> 00:02:03.191
One sketch showed a large wooden wheel.

30
00:02:03.192 --> 00:02:06.245
Another sketch was of a crane.

31
00:02:06.246 --> 00:02:10.951
"Machines built this cathedral," Leo replied.

32
00:02:10.952 --> 00:02:16.657
"To me machines are more fascinating than the buildings they make."

33
00:02:16.658 --> 00:02:22.580
Again Vinnie and Mandy were amazed at his talent.

34
00:02:22.581 --> 00:02:25.710
"Come inside," said Leo.

35
00:02:25.711 --> 00:02:29.999
"There are beautiful paintings and stained glass."

36
00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:34.191
As they followed Leo inside, Mandy whispered,

37
00:02:34.192 --> 00:02:37.739
"There's something special about Leo."

38
00:02:37.740 --> 00:02:42.298
"He's just a kid with talent," said Vinnie.

39
00:02:42.299 --> 00:02:46.051
"I don't think so, Vinnie," Mandy said.

40
00:02:46.052 --> 00:02:48.945
She stopped and looked around.

41
00:02:48.946 --> 00:02:53.367
"Vinnie! I think we're close to the end of our journey."

42
00:02:53.368 --> 00:02:57.207
They could see beautiful stained-glass windows.

43
00:02:57.208 --> 00:03:00.502
Tall arches curved above them.

44
00:03:00.503 --> 00:03:05.569
"I think this is the place in the photo," Mandy whispered.

45
00:03:05.570 --> 00:03:08.660
"Come look," Leo called.

46
00:03:08.661 --> 00:03:14.284
He sat, opened his notebook, and began to draw with his left hand.

47
00:03:14.285 --> 00:03:17.323
Mandy watched him sketch and said,

48
00:03:17.324 --> 00:03:20.653
"You're so talented!"

49
00:03:20.654 --> 00:03:24.570
"Even for a lefty?" Leo grinned.

50
00:03:24.571 --> 00:03:28.498
"Who cares if you are left-handed?" asked Vinnie.

51
00:03:28.499 --> 00:03:33.529
"Many people think left-handed people are weird," replied Leo.

52
00:03:33.530 --> 00:03:36.588
"But it doesn't bother me."

53
00:03:36.589 --> 00:03:41.101
He got up, leaving his notebook open on the floor.

54
00:03:41.102 --> 00:03:44.085
"I want to see some paintings in the dome,"

55
00:03:44.086 --> 00:03:47.026
he said and walked off.

56
00:03:47.027 --> 00:03:52.040
Mandy leaned over the open notebook and tried to read the writing.

57
00:03:52.041 --> 00:03:56.122
"I can't tell what it says," she said.

58
00:03:56.123 --> 00:04:02.995
"The writing is so strange!"
